  "nl_text": "The rschema_0430 database contains six tables, each with its own unique purpose. The user table stores information about the users of the system, including their email, full name, password, and other personal details. The attraction table contains information about the attractions available for booking, including their name, details, era, region, type, and reference price. The message table stores messages sent between users, along with the time they were sent and the user who sent them. The ticket_booking table tracks the bookings made by users for specific attractions, including the attraction ID, booking date, order status, and ticket quantity. The attraction_comment table stores comments left by users about specific attractions, along with the user ID and comment content. Finally, the attraction_favorite table stores information about which attractions are favorited by users, including the attraction ID, favorite creation time, and user ID. Each table has its own set of columns, with some columns serving as primary keys, foreign keys, or unique constraints. The database is designed to ensure data integrity and referential integrity, with each table referencing other tables through foreign keys and constraints.",
  "gold_question": "The system shall manage user basic information, including username, password, WeChat Open ID, name, QQ number, email, remarks, and the creation and update time of the account. The system shall also manage attraction information, including attraction name, details, reference price, images, era, type, region, and the creation and update time of the attraction. Users shall be able to book attraction tickets, with order information including user, attraction, booking date, ticket quantity, remarks, order status, and the creation and update time of the order. Users shall be able to comment on attractions, with comment information including user, attraction, comment content, review status, and the creation and update time of the comment. Users shall be able to leave messages on the platform, with message information including user, message content, and the creation and update time of the message. Additionally, users shall be able to favorite attractions of interest, with favorite information including user, attraction, and the creation and update time of the favorite.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_codellama13b/0430.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0430\nCREATE TABLE `user` (\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `email` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `full_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `password` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_id`),\n  UNIQUE KEY `email_UNIQUE` (`email`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `attraction` (\n  `attraction_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `details` text NOT NULL,\n  `era` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  `region` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  `type` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  `reference_price` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`attraction_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `message` (\n  `message_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `sender_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `recipient_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `content` text NOT NULL,\n  `sent_at` datetime NOT NULL DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`message_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `message_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`sender_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `message_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`recipient_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `ticket_booking` (\n  `booking_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `attraction_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `booking_date` datetime NOT NULL DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,\n  `order_status` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `ticket_quantity` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`booking_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `ticket_booking_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `ticket_booking_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`attraction_id`) REFERENCES `attraction` (`attraction_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `attraction_comment` (\n  `comment_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `attraction_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `comment_content` text NOT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`comment_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `attraction_comment_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `attraction_comment_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`attraction_id`) REFERENCES `attraction` (`attraction_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `attraction_favorite` (\n  `favorite_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `attraction_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`favorite_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `attraction_favorite_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `attraction_favorite_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`attraction_id`) REFERENCES `attraction` (`attraction_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
